class_name Moves
extends RefCounted
## Move data: timings, damage, cost and what the opponent can do about it.
## Each move's behavior lives in scripts/moves/ ("script"). Every balance number is here.
##   startup / active / recovery   seconds of wind-up, active phase and recovery
##   cost / cd                     energy and cooldown
##   damage, push (m/s), lift (m/s upward), stun (s), knocks_down, hitstop (impact pause)
##   strength                      0 light, 1 medium, 2 heavy (sound, rumble, effects)
##   poise                         while it winds up and runs, only hits with
##                                 strength >= move poise + Pokémon poise interrupt it
##                                 (0 by default: any hit from a light Pokémon cuts it)
##   needs_ground                  used in the air, the Pokémon dives and does it on landing
##   manual_aim                    continuous multi-hit streams (Hydro Pump, Flamethrower): the
##                                 player turns with the stick, no horizontal assist; the rival's
##                                 height is aimed automatically. manual_turn: how fast it turns.
##                                 Discrete attacks (single-hit beams, projectiles) aim themselves
##   cancels_dodge                 its recovery can be cancelled with a dodge
##   cancels_into_moves            if it lands, its recovery can be cancelled into another move
##   counterplay                   what the opponent can do (for design and the selection screen)
## Player-facing text (display_name, desc, counterplay) is in English and is translated
## through game/i18n/translations.csv.

